# Everything in here is a generated artefact tracked by DVC (see the `outs:` of
# dvc.yaml and the `outs` section of dvc.lock). Git must not also track them:
# if it did, the two systems would disagree about what a result is, and the
# usual `git add .` would quietly commit 180 MB of feature cache.
#
# Results are namespaced by `cache_tag` -- the released run writes to the
# top level, a smoke/CI run writes to reports/<tag>/ -- so ignore the whole
# directory rather than listing files one at a time.
/*
!/model_comparison.csv
!/.gitkeep
# `/*` above matches this file too, which would leave it untracked and make the
# whole rule disappear on a fresh clone.
!/.gitignore

# Figures are gitignored individually so the tracked placeholder survives.
/figures/*
!/figures/.gitkeep